(LST-34 — LANGUAGE.md:2369-2373 warns that `element N of` yields a
 REFERENCE to the child list, not a copy, so a child extracted before the
 parent reallocates "may point at freed memory". Probed at 5000 appends
 (far past any plausible growth threshold): the child stays intact and
 readable. The hazard is hedged ("may"), so this is not a discrepancy — but
 it is the one place in this section where the manual itself points at a
 use-after-free, and no leaf goes near it.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST-34.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   5003
   [2, 3]
   2
   2
)
